Intelligent Prefetching is fetching the right line at the right time by not evicting the wrong line.

The simplest way is to not use your head but pull loads from program and hoist them earlier on. 
You can either make it binding (aka provide destination for this new location) or just issue the load
in the hope it is at a closer location. For the latter dont allow cacheline spilling.

Dumb prefetching is speculating incorrectly :-) (rather than runahead which is issuing loads that would have 
happened a bit earlier) or evicting lines that are currently being used.

Chris Metcalf has an excellent tutorial here
